rom 3.449\n                                                                                                              layer at every frame, independently of the target bitrate. A\n                                          to 3.780 over matched fixed-depth coding.\n                                                                                                              constrained allocator then selects prefix-valid depths and ver-\n                                              Index Terms— neural speech coding, residual vec-                ifies the exact serialized size, including active indices, the\n                                          tor quantization, dynamic bit allocation, marginal utility,         run-length-coded depth map, the header, and byte padding.\n                                          variable-rate coding                                                The allocation is realized through prefix early exit and a\n                                                                                                              fully decodable dynamic bitstream, while the original codec\n                                                                                                              remains frozen.\n                                                                1. INTRODUCTION\n                                                                                                                   Our contributions are threefold. First, we introduce rate-\n                                          Neural speech codecs commonly combine learned encoder–              independent, frame- and layer-wise marginal-utility predic-\n                                          decoder architectures with residual vector quantization (RVQ)       tion for multiple operating rates. Second, we develop a\n                                          for high-quality compression at low bitrates [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].    bitstream-aware allocator with exact conta